sec-1-name = sec 1
chernyy-dnevnik-name = black diary
chernyy-dnevnik-desc = A small book in a plain, dense binding without any ornament. The pages are filled with an even, utterly emotionless hand. Anatomical diagrams and complex necromantic runes are sketched in the margins.
chernyy-dnevnik-content = [head=3][color=#4b0082]Observation Journal: Project "Ascension"[/color][/head]


    {"[italic]Cycle One. Vessel assessment.[/italic]"}

    {"Arrived at the count's invitation. Tissue condition of Subject \"L\" is satisfactory. Low temperatures in the crypt have slowed cellular decay. The count's grief makes him extremely compliant. He has granted full access to the dungeons and the garrison's resources. I begin the primary restructuring of the local arcane field. The residual aura of the local goddess, that pathetic Soma, still clings to the castle walls, but the emanations of Lord Morbius are rapidly driving out that Light."}


    {"[italic]Cycle Fourteen. Catalyst infusion.[/italic]"}

    {"Introduced concentrated necrotic solution into the Subject's halted circulatory system. Severe muscular spasms observed. The flesh resists the gift of Death, residual muscle memory activating. I increased ritual intensity."}

    {"[color=#a3a3a3]Side effect:[/color] the Morbius field breached the crypt shielding and began spreading through the castle. Flora withers, the water's structure shifts. The local garrison shows signs of early necrotic poisoning. This is useful. We will need obedient working hands."}


    {"[italic]Cycle Twenty-Nine. Metamorphosis of consciousness.[/italic]"}

    {"Had to put down two guards who stuck their noses into the laboratory. Used their biomaterial to stabilize Subject \"L\". The process proceeds faster than expected. The Subject's eyeballs have gone completely black, body temperature stabilized at absolute zero. She has begun responding to my voice."}


    {"[italic]Cycle Forty. Triumph.[/italic]"}

    {"[bold]Absolute success.[/bold] Subject \"L\" is functioning. Motor function and regeneration exceed those of a living human many times over."}


    {"The count was just here. He wept, kissed her icy hands, and swore eternal devotion. An unbelievable fool. He sees his precious wife in this vessel and entirely fails to notice that pure, hungry Abyss now pulses within her. She is no longer human. She is the Hierarch of our new Necropolis."}


    {"The castle fell without a single sword stroke. Now we need only wait until the corruption devours the whole island."}

promerzshiy-dnevnik-name = frozen diary
promerzshiy-dnevnik-desc = The pages of this small leather diary have grown hard and brittle from constant frost. The spine is covered with a thin crust of ice, and the paper gives off a grave-cold chill. The ink on the sheets has faded and run, as though the author wrote with shaking hands, occasionally breathing on the freezing quill.
promerzshiy-dnevnik-content = [color=#4a769e]The wind from the northern wastes howls enough to drive a man mad. The hearth has almost gone out, the firewood is frozen through and only hisses. I burn the last splinters, but this cold... it does not come from snow. It gets into the very bones, drawing out the soul.


    {"I saw them again. Tonight, there beyond the trees in the veil of snow. Pale silhouettes wandering through the blizzard. They leave no tracks, make no sound, not even when stepping over dry branches. Only their eyes... piercing, deathly blue [color=#00bfff]eyes, glowing in the dark[/color]."}


    {"My partner said they were only tales. That the dead sleep peacefully, and the flimsy walls of this watch hut would protect us. But the logs already crack from the cold. He did not wake this morning. Froze to death right on the bench, still holding his crossbow."}


    {"My fingers blacken with frostbite, and I can barely hold the quill. To keep from going mad with fear, I repeat the old motto of my house without stopping. Like a prayer. Like a spell."}


    {"[italic]Winter is coming.[/italic]"}

    {"[italic]Winter is coming.[/italic]"}


    {"Gods, save me... [color=#2c4a63]░░▒▓▓▓▒░░...[/color][/color]"}

staryy-dnevnik-name = old diary
roskoshnyy-dnevnik-name = luxurious diary
roskoshnyy-dnevnik-desc = A heavy book bound in black leather with a tarnished silver clasp. The pages are covered in an aristocrat's elegant hand, which toward the end turns into mad, ragged strokes. The paper smells of decay.
roskoshnyy-dnevnik-content = [head=3][color=#5a005a]Personal Chronicles of the Count[/color][/head]


    {"[italic]Day Six.[/italic]"}


    {"My priceless Liza is dead. That cursed fever devoured her in one miserable week. The vaunted physicians, those useless charlatans, only spread their hands and dared prattle of acceptance. They comforted me by saying Bright Soma would receive her soul into her halls... As if that could fill the ringing emptiness in my heart! A world without her smile is merely a crypt of cold stone. I will not give her to the worms. Her body has already been taken to the lower crypts and packed in ice. She is only sleeping."}


    {"[italic]Day Eighteen.[/italic]"}


    {"Mronemir has arrived. This man is strikingly unlike the pompous peacocks of the Collegium of Mages. In his eyes lies absolute understanding that death is not an end, but merely an unfortunate error in creation that can be corrected. Emperor Therion and his Legion may issue as many edicts banning necromancy as they wish. Their laws are not worth a broken copper when the return of my love is at stake. If merciful gods have turned away from us, I will make a bargain with Darkness itself without hesitation."}


    {"[italic]Day Forty.[/italic]"}


    {"The air in the castle has grown thick and cold. Servants pale, wither, and flinch from their own shadows. The captain of the guard cowardly reports panic in the garrison. Fools whisper of moans from the dungeons. Miserable, limited worms! They did not value her mercy in life, so let them now serve as material for her greatness. Mronemir assures me that Morbius himself, Lord of Death, has turned his gaze upon our lands. His influence seeps through the stones and soaks the soil. I feel his icy breath... and it is beautiful."}


    {"~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~"}

    {"~~~~~~~~~~ ............ ~~~~~~~~~~"}

    {"~~~~~~~~~~ ************ ~~~~~~~~~~"}

    {"~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~"}


    {"[color=#8b0000][bold]SHE OPENED HER EYES![/bold][/color]"}


    {"My Liza has returned to me! In her new gaze there is not a drop of former human weakness. Pure, primordial eternity shines within it. Frail flesh has given way to the perfection only death can grant. The power of Morbius pulses through her veins as black ichor, and I, her devoted husband, gladly bend the knee before the true Lord!"}


    {"My peasants shall become her silent servants, my guard her undead legion, knowing neither fear nor fatigue. We are no longer slaves to fate and the laws of the Empire. We are the true masters of this island."}


    {"[color=#8b0000][italic]Let this whole wretched world burn. We shall dance upon its ashes for all eternity.[/italic][/color]"}

drevniy-foliant-name = ancient folio
drevniy-foliant-desc = A heavy book bound in darkened, desiccated leather and drawn tight with tarnished metal clasps. The thick parchment pages feel unnaturally cold to the touch. The text is written in even, strict runes, with neither passion nor a call to blind faith, only the cold statement of the inevitable.
drevniy-foliant-content = [head=3]Testaments of the Evil God[/head]


    {"[italic]Man has no power even over his own will, for his very existence is but a fleeting convulsion in the endless shadow of the Eternal.[/italic]"}


    {"[bold]I. The Unity of Decay[/bold]"}

    {"All that possesses form strives toward dissolution. Rot is not an end, but the only true form of matter returning to its first repose. Fear not decomposition, for within it lies release from the fetters of changing life."}


    {"[bold]II. The Void as Cradle[/bold]"}

    {"Life is an unfortunate accident, sparks struck in the dark. Death is absolute order. Only when deprived of breath does the mind gain clarity, unclouded by the needs of flesh, and understand that silence is the highest form of speech."}


    {"[bold]III. The Primacy of Shadow[/bold]"}

    {"When the first stars had not yet been kindled, He already waited. When the last world turns to dust, He will remain. Time is sand running through the fingers of a dead man. It has no power over the One who created Darkness itself."}


    {"[bold]IV. Renunciation of the Existing[/bold]"}

    {"Abandon hope, for it blinds. Abandon fear, for it binds. Only one who admits his own insignificance before the face of the Evil God can become a vessel for His will. Become a shadow among shadows, part of the great host that knows neither weariness nor compassion."}

temnyy-foliant-name = dark folio
temnyy-foliant-desc = A heavy book covered in smooth, unnaturally black leather. The pages look frighteningly neat, without the slightest mark of time, damp, or dust. On the first page, strict instructions are written in perfect calligraphy, and the following pages contain even columns of names.
temnyy-foliant-content = [color=#8b0000][bold]RULES OF THE NOTEBOOK[/bold][/color]


    {"[italic]I.[/italic] A mortal whose true name is written upon these pages shall surely know the wrath of Morbius."}


    {"[italic]II.[/italic] The folio shall have no power if the writer does not clearly picture the victim's face at the moment of writing."}


    {"[italic]III.[/italic] If the cause of death is not specified within forty heartbeats, the victim shall fall from sudden cardiac arrest."}


    {"[italic]IV.[/italic] If the cause is specified, the writer has exactly six minutes and forty seconds more to inscribe the circumstances leading to the inevitable end."}


    {"[color=#555555]=========================================[/color]"}


    {"Baron Elmar of the Valley - [italic]cardiac arrest[/italic]"}


    {"Sergeant Gardner - [italic]fatal wound in a drunken brawl, choked on his own blood[/italic]"}


    {"Inquisitor Solus - [italic]cardiac arrest[/italic]"}


    {"Merchant █▒▓░ - [italic]fell from the scaffolding of his own unfinished estate, broken neck[/italic]"}


    {"[color=#555555]=========================================[/color]"}


    {"The thing from the realm of shadows that has followed me relentlessly since I broke the seal on the cover has not fallen silent for a single hour. Its dry laughter drives me mad. It is invisible to others, but I constantly feel its breath behind my back. The demon demands offerings. Who would have thought that heralds of death were so fond of simple red apples? I must buy another basket at the market, or I fear my own name will be next upon this list."}

potrepannyy-putevoy-zhurnal-name = battered travel journal
potrepannyy-putevoy-zhurnal-desc = The pages inside are surprisingly clean, and the author's hand is firm and paradoxically cheerful. The entries are written in warm golden-brown ink.
potrepannyy-putevoy-zhurnal-content = [color=#b8860b][head=2]Praise the Sun![/head]


    {"The sun is a wondrous light. Like a magnificent father! If only I could be so [color=#d4af37]incandescently radiant![/color]"}


    {"Does that seem strange to you? It should! Do not hide your reaction while reading these lines. Everyone looks at me that way! [italic]Ha-ha-ha![/italic]"}


    {"I left my home and came to these lands, this great cradle of lords, to seek my own sun. I cannot give up. I condemned myself to this path so that I might continue my search. My shield, my armor, are utterly ordinary. All my strength comes only from my [bold]faith[/bold]."}


    {"Time itself is illusory in these lands. And we are like two ships passing in the dark. Paths meet and part. Therefore, do not miss the chance to help your neighbor. Can anything be more beautiful than [italic]glorious cooperation?[/italic]"}


    {"If we meet, I will gladly come to your aid. Until then..."}

    {"[/color]"}

byust-neizvestnogo-dvoryanina-name = bust of an unknown nobleman
zalityy-sukrovitsey-pergament-name = ichor-soaked parchment
zalityy-sukrovitsey-pergament-desc = A rolled piece of stiff parchment found in road mud. It reeks of stale earth and alcohol fumes. The text is written crookedly, letters dancing as though the author wrote while running or shaking with fever.
zalityy-sukrovitsey-pergament-content = [head=3]The Silver Campaign[/head]

    {"[italic]"}

    {"Proud we marched toward the graves, all shining holy-bright,"}

    {"Father waved a piss-stained cloth and chanted with delight."}

    {"Said the dead would fear the light and crawl beneath the clay,"}

    {"Back into their deep old holes the moment we came their way."}


    {"But when we stepped into the crypt - [bold]Holy Mother save![/bold]"}

    {"Out there crawled a [color=#8a2be2]lich[/color] from the tomb, rattling bone from grave."}

    {"Licked the holy water clean, spat upon the icon,"}

    {"And death went walking through the crosses, feasting on the Legion."}


    {"A brawny knight with backsword high became a heap of dung:"}

    {"A [color=#a9a9a9]skeleton[/color] drove its jagged axe beneath him where it stung."}

    {"Father shrieked inside a puddle, kicking up his heels,"}

    {"While I crawled into the bushes after all my countrymen's squeals."}


    {"Dropped my shield and dropped my sword, cast off my dented helm,"}

    {"[bold]Devil take me if I march again into that realm![/bold]"}

    {"Let the holy rot in there with crosses, dust, and fear,"}

    {"I am running to the tavern, nearly died from terror here."}

    {"[/italic]"}

pomyatyy-pergament01-name = crumpled parchment
pomyatyy-pergament01-desc = A thin sheet of cheap gray parchment, long carried rolled up in a pocket. The text is written in faded ink, while the last lines were hurriedly drawn with a fine quill.
pomyatyy-pergament01-content = [color=#666666]...everything I managed to sell:[/color]


    {"[italic]Copper basin[/italic] - 4 coppers"}

    {"[italic]Warm boots[/italic] - 1 silver"}

    {"[italic]Mother's amulet[/italic] - 3 coppers"}


    {"The old miser in the shop swore the silver was false. Curse his head. This will not cover even half the levy. The collectors come tomorrow morning."}


    {"Marta, I took the knife and went to the old ruins beyond the road. They say the dead have no need of their gold. If I do not return by dawn -"}


    {"[bold]TAKE OUR SON AND RUN TO YOUR SISTER.[/bold]"}


    {"Open the door to no one."}

obryvok-pergamenta-name = scrap of parchment
obryvok-pergamenta-content = [head=3]Personal Notes I[/head]

    {"[color=#777777]██████▓▓▓▒▒▒░░░[/color]"}


    {"The guards no longer open the hatch. Those bony things simply throw rotten scraps through the bars. They do not care. They have no noses to smell the stench coming from my legs. The left limb has blackened and swollen up to the knee. At night rats come and gnaw the dead toes, and I have no strength even to drive them away. I am rotting alive in this cell, and no one will come to help. O Gods, be merciful, send me death faster than this leprosy devours me entirely."}

zalyapannyy-list01-name = stained sheet
zalyapannyy-list01-content = [head=3]Personal Notes II[/head]

    {"[color=#666666]██████▓▓▓▒▒▒░░░[/color]"}


    {"[italic]"}

    {"The pain is gone. Today I tried to tear the dried rags away from my shin. A great flap of dead flesh came off with them, revealing clean white bone. I thought I would go mad with horror, but instead I stared at it with enchanted calm."}


    {"There is no weakness in it. It does not fester, ache, or ask for food. It is perfect. Only now do I begin to understand the truth of the words with which they cast me into the dungeon. Flesh is merely a damp, stinking cage. And my cage is finally beginning to collapse."}

    {"[/italic]"}

protsarapannaya-zapiska-name = scratched note
protsarapannaya-zapiska-content = [head=3]Personal Notes III[/head]

    {"[color=#555555]██████▓▓▓▒▒▒░░░[/color]"}


    {"[italic]"}

    {"My right eye is gone. It ran out onto the stones. But in the darkness of the dungeon I see more clearly than I ever did beneath the sun. The dark is thick, tangible. It whispers that breath merely counts down the moments until decay. I stopped breathing yesterday, and I became so light. The pathetic human convulsion the living call a heartbeat has ended, giving way to absolute peace."}


    {"The skin on my hands comes off in strips. It only hinders my writing. I had to scrape it off against the wall. Far below, under the slabs of my tier, I hear a measured clatter. Those are my brothers."}


    {"I am no longer a prisoner. It is time to break out this grate."}

    {"[/italic]"}

parnyy-doklad-name = paired report
parnyy-doklad-desc = A scroll of dense parchment. The upper half is written in a quick, sharp hand, with some letters replaced by strange analogues. The second part has been added below, the letters formed with deliberate, almost painful elegance and aristocratic dignity despite smudged ink in places. The paper faintly smells of alchemical potions and carries a trace of healing magic.
parnyy-doklad-content = [head=3]Report on activity in the Necropolis[/head]


    {"Archmage."}


    {"We went after the scrolls for nothing. Your intelligence is useless. The Necropolis is under Dark Skeleton control. These are true followers of Morbius."}


    {"This is not mindless undead simply stomping around crypts. In the lower tiers, they have hammered together an army. We were surrounded by coordinated detachments. They struck with dark magic. Barely escaped. Mare took the blow so I could leave. He is under spells now. The wounds are foul, but healing magic is holding for the moment."}


    {"- Litora-Noxis."}


    {"[color=#555555]█████▓▓▒▒░[/color]"}


    {"[italic]Addendum:[/italic]"}


    {"The scrolls remain there, in the dark. The halls before the lower archives are literally packed with servants of the Evil God."}


    {"Understand this, Archmage: they are methodically forging their strength. And when the ritual of Morbius's resurrection begins at the Collegium altar, these dead legions will march as his merciless vanguard."}


    {"The healing charms are beneficial, and soon I will again regain the ability to hold a grimoire. Yet the sand in our hourglass is running out without mercy. If we do not bring our wrath down upon the Necropolis now, while their forces are only ripening, then on the day of their Lord's coming we will simply be wiped from the face of the earth."}


    {"- Mare-Messorem"}

promerzshiy-pergament-name = frozen parchment
promerzshiy-pergament-desc = A dense sheet of paper. The handwriting is even at the beginning, but by the end becomes twitching and illegible, and the final phrase breaks off in a blot.
promerzshiy-pergament-content = [head=2][color=#a3a3a3]Records of the Silver Campaign[/color][/head]


    {"[italic]Day Six.[/italic]"}


    {"The Light will show us the way. Tomorrow at dawn we march for the gates of the Necropolis. Our company has made camp in the grove, the fires burn bright, and our supplies will last through a long siege. The paladins raise prayers before the coming battle, and brothers-in-arms sharpen their blades. We are ready to cleanse the [bold]Abode of Morbius[/bold] of corruption and put an end to his godless rituals."}


    {"But with nightfall, this unnatural cold began to bite down to the very bones. The campfire no longer warms. Brother Thomas went to relieve himself half an hour ago and still has not returned."}


    {"The horses snort uneasily. One of the torches on the eastern side just went out. I hear a strange rustling of snow and the clatter of metal in the darkness between the trees."}


    {"[color=#8b0000][bold]They did not wait for our coming. They are already he[/bold][/color]"}

ispisannyy-pergament-name = written-over parchment
ispisannyy-pergament-desc = A dense sheet of old paper lying on the commander's table beside an inkwell. The text is written in a strict, sweeping hand, and the lower edge is stained with candle wax.
ispisannyy-pergament-content = [head=2]Vanguard Command Journal[/head]


    {"[italic]Commander Ewald. Position at the very Gates.[/italic]"}


    {"We have entrenched ourselves directly against the perimeter of the Necropolis. The engineering detachment has finished raising palisades, blocking the main approaches. From here the spire of Morbius's abode is already visible."}


    {"The fortifications are reliable, but proximity to the source of corruption is driving the men mad. For the second night in a row, sentries report shadows beyond the palisade, though the snow there is completely untouched. Provisions in the crates spoil with frightening speed, and the water tastes bitter. Yesterday two recruits threw down their weapons and tried to flee into the forest. We had to bind them so they would not freeze to death or fall to the dead."}


    {"[bold]Orders for the coming night:[/bold]"}

    {"- Double the guard at the gaps in the palisade."}

    {"- No one is to leave the camp perimeter, not even to piss. There are buckets for that."}

    {"- Anyone who speaks of \"whispers beneath the snow\" is to be sent to the chaplain at once."}


    {"We assault at dawn. If we delay even one more day, this cursed cold and fear will break our spirit. Either tomorrow we cleanse these lands, or we join the Lord's army."}

okrovavlennyy-pergament-name = bloodied parchment
okrovavlennyy-pergament-content = [head=3]Dispatch to Legion Command[/head]


    {"[italic]From the captain of the Count's garrison, Sir Wolfgang.[/italic]"}


    {"I write this with no particular illusions concerning your headquarters' swiftness, but regulations oblige me. I bring to your attention that our illustrious count has finally gone completely mad."}


    {"His precious wife passed from fever. Regrettable, I do not dispute it. Usually in such cases noble lords drink themselves blind or take young mistresses, but ours decided to challenge the natural order of things. He dragged a certain Mronemir into the castle. If that man is a learned physician, then I am the prima ballerina of the capital. He reeks of crypt from a mile away, and in the lower crypts bones now clatter around the clock and chemicals stink."}


    {"The situation has gone out of control. The castle is soaked in grave-cold, the wells are poisoned. My men are, shall we say, rapidly losing their human appearance. Literally. Yesterday the sentry on the eastern tower became covered in frost and stopped blinking. When I shouted to him, he only made a sound like an unoiled cart grinding."}


    {"This morning the count ordered half the garrison disarmed. Apparently to make it easier for Mronemir to spend them as materials for his tricks."}


    {"[bold]In summary:[/bold] we have a full-scale expansion of Morbius here."}


    {"Stop wearing out your trousers in endless meetings. Send a strike detachment. Preferably those who know how to swing a torch and heavy steel, not quote Imperial law. I will try to push the courier with this report beyond the gates under cover of night, but the chance that he does not join the army of the dead on the bridge is frankly small."}


    {"Move, before this filth spreads across the whole[color=#8b0000] island... ▓▒░[/color]"}

    {"[color=#8b0000]░▒▓██[/color][color=#660000]██▓▒░[/color]   [color=#8b0000]░▒▓█[/color]"}

    {"[color=#660000]▒▓███████▓▓▒[/color]  [color=#8b0000]▒▓██░[/color]"}

    {"[color=#4a0000]▓██████████▓▒░[/color] [color=#660000]▓██▒[/color]"}

    {"[color=#2b0000]██████████████▓▒[/color]"}

    {"[color=#1a0000]█████████████████[/color]"}

zasalennyy-pergament-name = greasy parchment
zasalennyy-pergament-desc = A rough sheet of paper heavily stained with wine and soot. The letters are crooked, and in places the quill has punched through the sheet from heavy pressure.
zasalennyy-pergament-content = [head=3]Stores Record. Lower Pantries.[/head]


    {"Written by me, Gustav."}


    {"[bold]Meat:[/bold] Three pig carcasses slaughtered the day before yesterday rotted by morning. Covered in black slime. Ordered them thrown into the moat, but the kitchen boy swears he saw one carcass move. Flogged him for lying, but I will not go down there again myself."}

    {"[bold]Vegetables:[/bold] Potatoes turned to gray dust. Root crops weep some sort of filth."}

    {"[bold]Wine:[/bold] Two barrels of Bordeaux have soured. Tastes like iron and old blood."}


    {"[italic]Note for the steward:[/italic]"}

    {"I refuse to work here. The trap I set by the wall for rats went off in the night. In the morning I went to check. The trap was shut, with a severed rat paw inside. And from the trap, a bloody trail leads away. [color=#a3a3a3]Toward the crack under the door. On three legs.[/color]"}


    {"There is no food in the castle. But there is plenty that wants to eat us. I resign. Let Lord Count eat his own rot."}

smyatyy-pergament01-name = crumpled parchment
smyatyy-pergament01-desc = A carelessly folded piece of dense paper smelling of cheap soap and stubborn cellar damp. The handwriting is small, cramped, and very hurried.
smyatyy-pergament01-content = [italic]Bright Soma, protect us.[/italic]


    {"I can no longer go down into the eastern wing. The master ordered me to clean Lady Liza's chambers, but when I approached the doors, such cold poured from within that the water in my bucket froze over with a crust of ice."}


    {"This new guest, Master Mronemir... flowers in tubs wither at the sound of his steps. Yesterday I saw him speaking with the groom. The groom stood with his back to me, and I called to him, but when he turned... [color=#8b0000]His eyes were white. Completely white, without pupils![/color] And he smiled so wide that the skin on his cheeks cracked."}


    {"I did not tell the housekeeper. She has not left her little room since yesterday and only mutters something about \"eternal service\"."}


    {"Tonight I will gather my things and leave through the back door. Better to freeze to death in the forest than stay in this cursed place. They say laughter of our late lady comes from the lower crypts at night... but the dead should not laugh like that."}

vyveska-taverna-snezhnyy-lis-name = "Snow Fox Tavern" sign
komnatnoe-rastenie-name = houseplant
komnatnoe-rastenie-desc = It does not look very healthy...

zolotaya-gravirovannaya-plita-name = golden engraved slab
zolotaya-gravirovannaya-plita-desc = WELCOME HOME. Flesh is weak and prone to disease. Swords rust. Empires crumble into dust. Only bone is beyond time. Only death is absolutely honest with all. Leave your fears behind as you cross this threshold. In the end, we will all be here.

statuya-suprugi-vladeltsa-imeniya-name = statue of the estate owner's wife
statuya-suprugi-vladeltsa-imeniya-desc = This statue commemorates the wife of the great lord. In the statue's hand rests a red velvet jewelry casket holding the jewels this beautiful woman loved.

sektor-1-nekropol-name = Sector 1 necropolis
sektor-1-tsentr-name = Sector 1 center
